   "daf": "47a",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "הָיוּ שְׁנֵיהֶן חֲשׁוּדִין. אֲמַר לֵיהּ רָבָא לְרַב נַחְמָן: הֵיכִי תְּנַן? אֲמַר לֵיהּ: לָא יָדַעְנָא. הִלְכְתָא מַאי? אֲמַר לֵיהּ: לָא יָדַעְנָא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If «both» litigants «were suspect,» the oath returned to its place; this is the statement of Rabbi Yosei. Rabbi Meir says: Since neither can take an oath, they divide the disputed amount. «Rava said to Rav Naḥman: How is it» actually «taught?» What is Rabbi Yosei’s opinion and what is Rabbi Meir’s opinion? Rav Naḥman «said to him: I do not know.» Rava asked him: «What is the halakha?» Rav Naḥman «said to him: I do not know.»"
  }
 ],
